 "result": "The failing call is at `src/tessel/sessions.py:374`, inside `persist_session`. It's the `response.set_cookie(...)` call:\n\n```python\nresponse.set_cookie(\n    name,\n    val,\n    expires=expires,\n    httponly=httponly,\n    domain=domain,\n    path=path,\n    secure=secure,\n    partitioned=partitioned,\n    samesite=samesite,\n)\n```\n\nThe rejected argument is **`partitioned=partitioned`**. Werkzeug 3.0.3's `Response.set_cookie()` has no `partitioned` parameter, so it raises `TypeError: Response.set_cookie() got an unexpected keyword argument 'partitioned'`.\n\nThe same keyword is also passed to `response.delete_cookie(...)` earlier in `persist_session`, which would fail the same way on 3.0.3. The failing tests only reach the `set_cookie` call.",
